WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.350
A million names, in alphabetical order.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.790
Somewhere in there is the one you need.

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.010
Start at the top.

4
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.130
Check a name.

5
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.050
Not it.

6
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.290
Check the next.

7
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.170
If your name is near the end,
that could take a million checks.

8
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.790
Yet 20 checks are always enough.

9
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.190
Not 20 thousand.

10
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.650
Just 20.

11
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.410
How can 20 checks find
one name among a million?

12
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.310
In this mission, you'll
start with the simple way:

13
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.010
a linear search checks each item in turn,

14
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.290
from the first.

15
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.210
Then you'll see why it
matters that a list is sorted,

16
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.570
like a dictionary.

17
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.480
Your mission: work out how
so few checks can be enough.
